From 6a389db51473ad892a451d893d1934136a04a3c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 23:13:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/52] util/os_misc: query available memory through sysconf
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

os_get_available_system_memory() reads /proc/meminfo on Linux, sysctl on
the BSDs, mach on Apple, GlobalMemoryStatusEx on Windows — and returns
false everywhere else. _SC_AVPHYS_PAGES answers the same question
portably and is already how os_get_total_physical_memory() and
os_get_page_size() get theirs a few lines away, so use it as the last
resort before giving up.

Guarded on HAVE_SYSCONF *and* on _SC_AVPHYS_PAGES being defined: the
name is a common extension (glibc, Solaris, and others) rather than
base POSIX, so a C library with sysconf but without it keeps the
existing "return false". Placed after every existing branch, so no
platform that answers today changes how it answers.

"Available" is deliberately not "free": _SC_AVPHYS_PAGES is defined as
the pages currently available to a process, which is the same quantity
MemAvailable and HW_USERMEM approximate on the branches above.

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 3 item 6 (physical memory / page size queries)
Why: without this the function returns false on Horizon, which is not
  the harmless "unknown" it looks like. NVK installs it as the sysmem
  heap's budget callback (nvk_physical_device.c:1556), so heapBudget
  for that heap comes out 0 — and on a Tegra SoC it is the *only* heap
  — violating the VK_EXT_memory_budget clause the code itself quotes
  three lines further down at nvk_physical_device.c:1725, plus a
  vk_loge on every vkGetPhysicalDeviceMemoryProperties2 call.
  Allocators such as VMA read heapBudget and conclude there is no
  allocatable memory.
Evidence: the pre-existing "#else return false" at the end of the
  function is the branch Horizon takes; this project's compat/ sysconf
  answers _SC_AVPHYS_PAGES from svcGetInfo(InfoType_TotalMemorySize)
  minus svcGetInfo(InfoType_UsedMemorySize).
Upstream: yes — general, guarded on the macro actually existing, and
  strictly a new last resort.
---
 src/util/os_misc.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/util/os_misc.c b/src/util/os_misc.c
index cc2248f1ca8..6173e228714 100644
--- a/src/util/os_misc.c
+++ b/src/util/os_misc.c
@@ -477,6 +477,15 @@ os_get_available_system_memory(uint64_t *size)
 
    *size = ((uint64_t)vm_stats.free_count + (uint64_t)vm_stats.inactive_count) * PAGE_SIZE;
    return true;
+#elif HAVE_SYSCONF && defined(_SC_AVPHYS_PAGES)
+   const long avail_pages = sysconf(_SC_AVPHYS_PAGES);
+   const long page_size = sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE);
+
+   if (avail_pages <= 0 || page_size <= 0)
+      return false;
+
+   *size = (uint64_t)avail_pages * (uint64_t)page_size;
+   return true;
 #else
    return false;
 #endif
